+# NVIDIA + Aegis Integration Playbook
+
+This document outlines the artifacts in this patch and how to use them to run the Pilots:
+
+Pilots included:
+- A) Triton model promotion pipeline (CI build/sign/attest, Triton model repo registration, Argo deploy workflow, Gatekeeper/Governance).
+- B) DGX/EGX/Triton deployment scaffolds (runtimeclass, triton deployment with GPU nodeSelector, seccomp PSP).
+- C) Morpheus → Aegis connector (ingest connector, verifier stub, A2A connector).
+- D) Operator playbook and runbooks (this doc).
+
+Quick start (recommended):
+1. Configure secrets in your repo: REGISTRY_URL, REGISTRY_USER, REGISTRY_TOKEN, COSIGN_PRIVATE_KEY/COSIGN_PUB_KEY, REKOR_URL.
+2. Deploy Gatekeeper & cert-manager to your cluster.
+3. Deploy the model-provenance webhook with cert-manager-signed TLS; run in audit (failurePolicy=Ignore).
+4. Run the CI workflow by pushing a model commit to main; verify cosign/Rekor artifacts.
+5. Provision GPU nodepool and label nodes with node-role.kubernetes.io/gpu=true.
+6. Deploy triton-server and create PVC for model repo; run Argo deploy workflow to register/push model repo.
+7. Deploy Morpheus connector; point Morpheus to the ingest endpoint.
+
+Notes & next steps:
+- Replace stubbed implementations with production operators (KMS encryption, S3/MinIO, Triton model conversion steps, onboarding to Fleet Manager).
+- Harden webhook & Gatekeeper policies and run 48–72h audit before switching to Fail.
+- Integrate MLflow model metadata (latency, precision, cosign attestation URL) into promotion guard.
